## AI-Assisted

## Per-account polyinstantiation of shared, world-writable temporary
## directories using pam_namespace. Drop-in; parsed after the libpam-modules
## default /etc/security/namespace.conf.
##
## Goal: a user must not see, read, race, or predict another account's temp
## files in /tmp, /var/tmp, /dev/shm. libpam-tmpdir only sets $TMPDIR and is
## bypassed by any program that hardcodes /tmp - pam_namespace gives a real
## private mount, so hardcoded /tmp is isolated too.
##
## Columns: polydir  instance_prefix  method[:flags]  excluded_users
##   - method 'user'  -> one instance per account, shared across that account's
##                       sessions, persists (on-disk backing).
##   - method 'tmpfs' -> a fresh empty RAM-backed instance per session; mntopts
##                       hardens the mount independently of remount-secure.
##   - excluded users 'root,adm' keep the shared dirs for system/daemon logins.
##
## Rationale per directory:
##   /tmp     tmpfs - keep it RAM-only (anti-forensics); nothing in /tmp is
##            meant to survive a session. noexec is intentionally NOT set,
##            because some programs legitimately execute from /tmp.
##   /var/tmp user  - FHS: persists across reboots; per-account on-disk instance.
##   /dev/shm tmpfs - RAM-only POSIX shared memory; fresh per session.
##
## iscript on /tmp recreates the X11/ICE socket dirs inside the fresh instance
## (see pam-namespace-init). $HOME is deliberately NOT polyinstantiated - that
## would hide the user's own data and only makes sense on SELinux MLS systems.
##
## The instance_prefix field is mandatory but is UNUSED by the tmpfs method
## (it mounts a fresh filesystem, not a dir under the prefix); the /tmp-inst/
## and /dev/shm-inst/ values below are placeholders and no such dir is created.
## Only the user-method /var/tmp has a real instance parent (/var/tmp/tmp-inst,
## created 0000 root:root via tmpfiles.d 30_security-misc-polyinstantiation).
##
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Dev/Strong_Linux_User_Account_Isolation
## man namespace.conf

/tmp       /tmp-inst/          tmpfs:mntopts=nosuid,nodev:iscript=/usr/libexec/security-misc/pam-namespace-init   root,adm
/var/tmp   /var/tmp/tmp-inst/  user   root,adm
/dev/shm   /dev/shm-inst/      tmpfs:mntopts=nosuid,nodev   root,adm
